Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a conversation whose client took the images of
 earlier turns out goes on in its run (#5612)

A client that strips the images of turns before the last one out
between turns (WorkBuddy) sent a conversation whose key no run had:
the images a client took out were told from any other change in the
last turn alone (looseTurn.rewrote, #1382), while the earlier turns'
were in the looseTurn key's hash, so a new turn after such a strip
found no run and no lost record (the run's, keyed by keys the
conversation had before the strip), and a new Claude Code was told
the whole conversation in one message, a prefix the cache had seen
only up to the taken-out image: cache_read fell back to the system
prompt's size (previous_message_not_found) and the whole history was
written again. WorkBuddy's images flip 1-0-1-3-0 between turns; a
Claude subscription's hit rate fell to 92%.

looseTurn keeps the whole conversation as heardRuns too (whole), and
rewritten takes a run, or a saved session, whose conversation the
request's is with the images of earlier turns taken out and nothing
else changed (lostMedia over the whole, mediaLost), as follows and
rewrote already took the images of the results and the last turn. A
conversation whose words changed is never this. The log says which
rewrite went on, in its run or from its saved session.

Tests: TestClaudeTurnAfterTheImagesOfEarlierTurnsTakenOutGoesOnInItsRun,
an image taken out and one replaced by the line going on in the run
that had them, told the new turn alone, and the user's words changed
still starting anew.

